# .env — copy this file to `.env` and uncomment what you need. NEVER committed (see .gitignore).
#
# ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │  You need NOTHING here to start: `npm run sandbox` (no key) and `npm run first-site` (your Claude │
# │  subscription through Claude Code) work with an empty environment. Everything below is OPTIONAL.  │
# └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
# The NAME of each variable is fixed by the code: write it EXACTLY (UPPERCASE, no space around the =, quotes only
# when the value contains a space). Only the VALUE is yours. Reference of every variable: docs/CONFIGURATION.md.
# Check your machine any time: `npm run doctor` (getting started) · `npm run doctor -- --for agency` (always-on).

# ── SHARED DATABASE (optional: a worker on another machine, a CRM shared between machines, the always-on agency) ─────
# Without it, `npm run backoffice` keeps its own local database on this machine (data/pglite, nothing to install):
# Find prospects, the call list and the jobs work. `npm run first-site` needs no database at all.
# Any Postgres 14+ (docker, Neon, Supabase…). Create the schema: `npm run db:init` (idempotent).
# Local docker one-liner: docker run -d --name lws-pg -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=lws -p 5432:5432 postgres:17-alpine
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:lws@127.0.0.1:5432/postgres
# Supabase on IPv4 (most machines): use the POOLER URL in session mode (Settings → Database → Connection pooling).
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
# TLS to the database: disable | require | prefer | verify-full. Default: require, except on 127.0.0.1/localhost.
# DB_SSL=require
# Connection pool size per process (default 4 for the cockpit, 10 for scripts; the sandbox uses 1).
# DB_POOL_MAX=4
# Supabase service_role key, only to upload media to a Storage bucket. Optional.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=eyJ...

# ── MODELS: BRING YOUR SUBSCRIPTION (packages/llm; guide: docs/BYO-MODEL.md) ──────────────────────────────────
# Default: everything runs on YOUR Claude subscription through Claude Code (`claude -p`). Nothing to set.
# The skills (prospect sheet, visual gate, sales mail…) go through the way you pick here:
#   claude-code (default) | codex (your ChatGPT subscription) | anthropic (Claude API key)
#   | anthropic-compatible (Ollama, LM Studio, LiteLLM, a gateway) | openai-compatible (OpenAI, OpenRouter, Groq, vLLM…)
# The agents that BUILD the sites always run in Claude Code (a Claude subscription, Pro or Max).
# LWS_LLM=claude-code
# ChatGPT subscription: `npm i -g @openai/codex` then `codex login`. The product REMOVES OPENAI_API_KEY from every
# `codex exec` (otherwise Codex would bill the API instead of your subscription). Model: your CLI's default unless set.
# LWS_LLM=codex
# LWS_CODEX_BIN=codex
# Legacy switch, still understood: LLM_VIA=plan (→ claude-code) | api (→ anthropic).
# LLM_VIA=plan
#
# Models by ROLE (defaults: Opus 5.5 / Haiku 5.5 / Sonnet 5.5 on the API; the aliases opus / haiku / sonnet on a
# subscription, which follow your Claude Code version). smart = builds and writes; fast = reads a site into a
# prospect sheet; judge = looks at screenshots (gate, blind judge). The value is passed as is.
# LWS_MODEL_SMART=claude-opus-5-5
# LWS_MODEL_FAST=claude-haiku-5-5
# LWS_MODEL_JUDGE=claude-sonnet-5-5
# One model for every role (typical of a local model):
# LWS_MODEL=llama3.2:1b
# Thinking effort per role on the Claude API (low | medium | high | xhigh | max; default: the model's own):
# LWS_EFFORT_FAST=low
#
# Claude API key (platform.claude.com → API keys), billed per token. The SDK 1.x sends it as `Authorization: Bearer`.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# Any server that speaks the Messages API. Ollama (≥ 0.14):
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=ollama
# Any Chat Completions server (OPENAI_API_KEY optional for a local one):
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# OPENAI_MODEL=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
#
# Subscription on a server with no browser: `claude setup-token`, then
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=...
# (The product REMOVES ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from every `claude -p`: in -p, Claude Code would prefer it to your plan.)

# ── MEDIA / GENERATIVE AI (optional: without them the composer keeps the prospect's real photos) ───────────────
# Images: OpenAI Images, direct (worker/openai-image.mjs). Engine: openai | none. Default: openai when
# OPENAI_API_KEY is set, otherwise none.
# LWS_IMAGE=none
# Key from platform.openai.com/api-keys (also used by the openai-compatible way when OPENAI_BASE_URL is empty).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# Base of a compatible Images API (default https://api.openai.com/v1) and model (default gpt-image-2).
# OPENAI_IMAGE_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-2
# Hero video: higgsfield | none. Default: higgsfield when HIGGSFIELD_API_KEY is set or the `higgsfield` CLI is on the
# PATH (Ultra account), otherwise none.
# LWS_VIDEO=none
# HIGGSFIELD_API_KEY=...
# (optional) API base and video model; the lines show the defaults (what you are billed for if you change nothing).
# HIGGSFIELD_API_BASE=https://api.higgsfield.ai
# HF_VIDEO_MODEL=kling3_0_turbo
# ⚠ Every video generated through the API or the MCP SPENDS credits. Do not count on an "unlimited" plan here: the
# unlimited Seedance offer covers the Higgsfield website only, never the API.

# ── SUPABASE STORAGE (optional; derived / sane defaults) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPABASE_URL is DERIVED from DATABASE_URL when absent; the default bucket comes from agency.config.json.
# SUPABASE_KEY is accepted as an alias of SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_BUCKET=lastwebstudios-assets
# Public base URL of a self-hosted media server (takes priority over Supabase Storage).
# ASSETS_BASE_URL=

# ── COCKPIT / NOTIFICATIONS (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The cockpit (npm run backoffice). Password = Basic auth, to protect remote access.
# BACKOFFICE_PASSWORD=
# BACKOFFICE_PORT=4000
# With no DATABASE_URL, npm run backoffice keeps its own local database in data/pglite (Find prospects, the call
# list and the jobs work on a laptop). 0 = go without (the cockpit then reads output/ only).
# LWS_LOCAL_DB=1
# Telegram review bot: @BotFather → /newbot → token.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123456:ABC-...
# Allow-list of the chats the bot serves (comma-separated ids; a group has a negative id).
# EMPTY = the bot serves NOBODY (closed by default). Write to the bot: it logs your id; add it here.
# TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_CHAT_IDS=123456789

# ── DEPLOYMENT HOOK (on your server only) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# COOLIFY_DEPLOY_HOOK=http://<server>:8000/api/v1/deploy?uuid=<APP_UUID>&force=false
# COOLIFY_TOKEN=

# ── OUTREACH (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LIVE email sending: 1 = allowed. Absent = test mode everywhere (the sequencer AND the warmup only log).
# The sequencer ALSO requires "dryRun": false in outreach/sequencer/config.json (two switches).
# LWS_LIVE_SEND=1
# Recipient of the warmup's daily digest (`npm run warmup -- digest`). REQUIRED for the digest: no default.
# DIGEST_FROM = sending mailbox (default: the first mailbox of pool B).
# DIGEST_TO=ops@agency.example
# DIGEST_FROM=
# French company registry (public API, free): 0 disables the call; LWS_SIRENE_URL replaces the URL (tests).
# LWS_SIRENE=1
# OUTREACH_SITE_BASE=     # public link of the new site when hosted elsewhere
# OUTREACH_DEMO=1         # 0 disables the demo video
# OUTREACH_FROM_NAME=

# ── SELF-HOSTED TRACKING (clicks + one-click unsubscribe, served by the cockpit under /t/; outreach/tracking/README.md)
# BOTH are required: without them no link is rewritten and unsubscribing happens by a "STOP" reply + mailto.
# TRACK_BASE = the PUBLIC URL of the cockpit (https in production): it is what appears in the mails.
# LWS_TRACK_SECRET = at least 32 characters (openssl rand -base64 48). The same on the cockpit AND the sequencer.
# TRACK_BASE=https://cockpit.agency.example
# LWS_TRACK_SECRET=
# Reply reader of the sequencer: gmail (read-only Gmail API, default when outreach/sequencer/sa-key.json exists)
# | file (data/sequencer/inbox.jsonl, for rehearsals) | none (replies marked by hand).
# LWS_REPLY_READER=gmail
# Transport of LIVE mails: gmail (default) | simulated (logs to data/sequencer/transport.jsonl, sends nothing).
# LWS_SIMULATED_FAIL=<text>: the simulated transport fails for those recipients (rehearsals).
# LWS_MAIL_TRANSPORT=simulated

# ── THE 24/7 CAGE (npm run cage; packages/shared/cage.ts) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Emergency STOP: a STOP file at the root (`npm run cage -- stop "reason"`, or the button in the cockpit).
# LWS_STOP_FILE=STOP
# Spend cap in $ per UTC day, all spending (claude -p agents, skills, images, videos; data/logs/spend.jsonl).
# Absent = no cap. Reached = no job is claimed until midnight UTC. On a subscription these are estimates, not bills.
# Set it before anything unattended: Hands-off refuses to turn on without it (the cockpit's Hands-off sheet sets it).
# LWS_BUDGET_USD_DAY=20
# Cap in $ of ONE agent job (passed as --max-budget-usd, bounded by what is left today).
# LWS_JOB_MAX_USD=6
# Estimated cost of an image / a video when the provider returns no price (conservative defaults).
# LWS_IMAGE_USD=0.25
# LWS_VIDEO_USD=1.50
# How often a running agent checks for STOP (ms).
# WORKER_STOP_POLL_MS=5000

# ── YOUR AGENCY and the sandbox ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The agency's identity (name, country, language, legal mail footer, HELO, User-Agent, invoices, sales mail facts,
# CRM operators) lives in agency.config.json (fictional examples: agency.config.example.json, .us.json). To read
# another file:
# LWS_AGENCY_CONFIG=agency.config.example.us.json
# HELO of the SMTP verifier (default: mail.heloDomain of agency.config.json):
# VERIFY_HELO=your-domain.example
# `npm run sandbox` needs NO variable: embedded database (PGlite), fictional agency, nothing goes out.
